# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is committed on purpose: this workspace ships binary apps
# (rdesktop-cli, rdesktop-dev, the examples) and needs reproducible,
# lock-step builds across machines. Remove this only if the repo becomes a
# pure library with no binary targets.

# rcode sub-repo (independent git repository living inside this checkout)
rcode/

